{"name":"Vape Smoke","hex":"#e8e8d7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of vaporizer.","An electronic cigarette."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale the vapor produced by a non-combustible cigarette, most commonly an electronic cigarette."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vape"},{"term":"smoke","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The visible vapor/vapour, gases, and fine particles given off by burning or smoldering material.","A cigarette."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale and exhale the smoke from a burning cigarette or cigar, burning material in a pipe, etc.","To inhale and exhale tobacco smoke."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electronic cigarette","blocks":[{"text":"An electronic cigarette (e-cigarette) or vape is a device that simulates tobacco smoking. It consists of an atomizer, a power source such as a battery, and a container such as a cartridge or tank. Instead of smoke, the user inhales vapor, often called \"vaping\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/CDC_electronic_cigarettes_October_2015_%28cropped%29.png/330px-CDC_electronic_cigarettes_October_2015_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_cigarette"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"im